<title>NETHERLANDS: Hoogovens talks with unions break down.</title>
<headline>Hoogovens talks with unions break down.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-02-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Talks between management and unions at Dutch steel and aluminium group Hoogovens NV over job cuts have broken down and strike action is now likely, Dutch news agency ANP said on Saturday.</p>
<p>Hoogovens Steel wants to discharge 3,000 of its 10,500 employees and recruit 1,000 new, highly-trained young workers.</p>
<p>Management has refused to guarantee demands that there should be no compulsory redundancies as part of the move and ANP quoted a union spokesman saying industrial action was now almost certain unless negotiations could be restarted. -- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
</text>
